Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 05:54:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 034/154] feat: delete the content_shell Atrium arm and the
 third frozen bridge copy
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

content/shell/browser/atrium_bridge.h was the third copy of
the frozen vtable, kept byte-identical with the Swift one. Its only consumer
was atrium_tab_host, which dlopen'd the dylib to host a SwiftUI sidebar in the
M1 content_shell fallback.

With the dylib gone, TabHost::connected() is permanently false, so all five
guards took their else path. Removed rather than stubbed: the shared-window tab
model, the Cmd+W tab-close override, the DestroyShell keep-open path, the
sidebar hosting and the frame inset, plus Shell::atrium_active_shell and
ShellPlatformDelegate::AtriumShowShell.

content_shell builds with no errors and no new warnings. content/shell now
contains no reference to Atrium at all.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
